  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>As compound,&nbsp;A instantly reacts with lucas reagent it should be a tertiary alcohol, and&nbsp;&nbsp;A&nbsp; a&nbsp;tertiaryl alcohol is formed by the reaction of grignard reagent,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mi>MgBr</mi></math>&nbsp;with&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>8</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>8</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math>,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>8</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>8</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math>&nbsp; should be a ketone and based on the formula it can be identified as a aromatic ketone.</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/27ba31ad-c681-4df3-8501-9ad33fe9e346-2018org.png\" style=\"width: 530px; height: 184px;\" /></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p></blockquote>",
